> Servings: 5

= Ingredients

@olive oil{3/8%cup}\
@minced fresh rosemary{1 1/4%teaspoon}\
@fresh lemon juice{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@red wine vinegar{1 1/4%tablespoon}\
@finely grated lemon peel{3 1/8%teaspoons}\
@salt{1 7/8%teaspoons}\
@ground black pepper{5/8%teaspoon}\
@medium head of cauliflower, trimmed, cut into small florets (about 3 cups){1 1/4}\
@(15-ounce) can white beans (such as Great Northern or navy beans), drained{1 1/4}\
@large heads of Belgian endive, trimmed, halved lengthwise, then thinly sliced crosswise{2 1/2}\
@chopped fresh chives{1 1/4%tablespoon}\
@chopped fresh parsley{2 1/2%teaspoons}\
@crumbled feta cheese (about 3 ounces){5/8%cup}

= Directions
Combine oil and rosemary in small saucepan. Stir over medium heat just until fragrant, about 1 minute. Cool.

Whisk lemon juice, vinegar, lemon peel, salt, and pepper in small bowl.

Combine cauliflower, beans, endive, chives, parsley, and rosemary oil in medium bowl; toss. Mix in cheese. Add lemon juice mixture and toss to coat. Season salad with salt and pepper.
